1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
残酷な天使のように 少年よ 神話になれ

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:29,000
青い風が今 胸のドアを叩いても

3
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:37,000
私だけをただ見つめて 微笑んでるあなた

4
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:44,000
そっと触れるもの 求めることに夢中で

5
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:52,000
運命さえまだ知らない 痛い気な瞳

6
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
だけどいつか気づくでしょう その背中には

7
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:07,000
遥か未来 目指すための羽があること

8
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:15,000
残酷な天使の帝世 窓辺からやがて飛び立つ

9
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,000
おとばしる熱いパトスで 思い出を裏切るなら

10
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,000
この空を抱いて輝く 少年よ 神話になれ

11
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
ご視聴ありがとうございました

12
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,000
ご視聴ありがとうございました

13
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
ご視聴ありがとうございました

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
初めての工場に 恐れるものと

15
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
簡単に誘うお値しください

16
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,000
ご視聴ありがとうございました

17
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,000
ご視聴ありがとうございました

18
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,000
ちゃんと祝аковを版 like

19
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
されたら 有賊はあり返し

20
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,000
その通りに確認 對し

21
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,600
That will be blocked any day now.

22
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:52,380
So should I do something about that project as well?

23
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:55,960
No. Judging by the material you sent me, it appears there will be no need.

24
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:57,560
Then I'll proceed with the plan.

25
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:11,980
Uh, good morning.

26
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:17,020
Good morning.

27
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:28,480
That's the way to start your morning.

28
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:30,520
What's wrong with coffee?

29
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:32,400
You got a problem with tradition?

30
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:37,540
Don't you know that a traditional Japanese breakfast is steamed rice, miso soup, and a little sake?

31
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,100
Your tradition, maybe.

32
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:40,360
Excuse me?

33
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:44,640
And incidentally, just whose turn was it supposed to be to cook today?

34
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:48,080
Well, now I know why a woman your age is still single.

35
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:50,480
You're going to be an old maid, miso.

36
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:52,340
Are you saying that I'm lazy?

37
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,120
And sloppy, too.

38
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:56,060
Oh, just leave me alone.

39
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,320
Oh, I'm finished.

40
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:02,680
So, are you really coming to my school today?

41
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:04,000
Of course I am.

42
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,900
It's your parent-teacher meeting.

43
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:08,000
But you're just so busy at work.

44
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,460
Oh, it's no problem.

45
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,800
You're part of my job anyway.

46
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:12,940
Well, it's just part of your job, huh?

47
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:16,940
Hi!

48
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,360
Oh, thanks for coming.

49
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:20,740
Yes, he's getting ready.

50
00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:22,440
I'll come let you in.

51
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:25,820
Misato, you shouldn't go outside dressed like that.

52
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,260
It's embarrassing.

53
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:28,420
I know.

54
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:33,240
Good morning, Ikari.

55
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:34,520
Thanks, Misato.

56
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,360
We're taking off now.

57
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:37,220
Be careful.

58
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:41,180
Oh, come on.

59
00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:46,260
Ironic.

60
00:03:46,820 --> 00:03:50,060
The way he's getting more casual and expressing his feelings is a good trend.

61
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:58,620
Yes, he's just left.

62
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:00,620
Make sure you keep your eyes on him.

63
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:12,580
Yeah!

64
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:14,080
Oh, she really came!

65
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:23,720
Is she Ikari's guardian?

66
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:24,320
What?

67
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:26,860
He's got a babe like that for a bodyguard?

68
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:27,720
Look at those idiots.

69
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:32,600
Oh, Misato is so gorgeous.

70
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:33,820
Yeah, right.

71
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:37,560
It's amazing someone so beautiful could be Nerve's operations director.

72
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:38,920
I don't think so.

73
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:39,620
Huh?

74
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:41,660
Hey, Kensuke.

75
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:43,580
It's a good thing that Shinji is such a baby.

76
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,260
Yeah, he's no rival for us.

77
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:49,920
You guys don't know what a slob she is.

78
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:53,380
Man, I wish Misato were my girlfriend.

79
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,760
Oh, no, you don't.

80
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:58,300
You just don't get it, do you?

81
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:03,380
Okay, you can handle keeping the Earth safe, and the two of us will take care of Misato.

82
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:09,480
Unit 1 has achieved the required cooling level.

83
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:10,580
Shifting operations to stage 2.

84
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:11,600
Keeping the Earth safe.

85
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:13,300
That's what Eva's for.

86
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:16,640
Come to think of it, just what is Eva?

87
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:19,580
This entry plug smells a lot like blood.

88
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:22,540
But I feel so comfortable and relaxed here.

89
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:26,140
Now that I think of it, I don't know anything about it.

90
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:29,200
What's the status of Unit 0's bio-chest components?

91
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:35,160
It was seriously damaged, so we'll have to make an entirely new one, even though it's pretty close to our ancillary budget's limits.

92
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:38,300
Will our job get any simpler once we get Unit 2 from Germany?

93
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,600
It could go just the other way.

94
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:43,020
Disposing of those dead angels costs a bundle.

95
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:48,360
Yeah, this place is ridiculously underfinanced, especially since mankind's future rests on us.

96
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:49,500
It can't be helped.

97
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:51,580
Man cannot live by Eva alone.

98
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:53,900
All those survivors need money to live, too.

99
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,480
Money, money, money.

100
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:58,480
So is the commander off to another conference again?

101
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:00,480
Yes, he's on board and in route now.

102
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:02,660
Thank God for a little peace and quiet.

103
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:14,760
Excuse me, do you mind if I sit here?

104
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:15,600
Go ahead.

105
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:21,700
The revised budget for the sample collection passed quite easily, didn't it?

106
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:24,480
The committee's main concern is for their own survival.

107
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:27,900
They won't be so budget conscious when their own lives are at stake.

108
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:30,620
Yes, they used to think they were no more angels.

109
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:32,660
And I have more good news.

110
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:39,060
All the permanent members of the Security Council, except the United States, have approved the budget for AVA Unit 6.

111
00:06:39,620 --> 00:06:42,360
It's just a matter of time before the U.S. approves it as well.

112
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:46,240
The Americans seem to be allergic to unemployment, but they'll learn.

113
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,060
And your country?

114
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:51,760
We will participate in the construction beginning with Unit 8.

115
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:55,000
The plans for the second installation project are still viable.

116
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:57,660
However, a pilot has not yet been found.

117
00:06:58,280 --> 00:06:59,560
The Angels have returned.

118
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:03,640
We will have no other choice but to defeat them.

119
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:06,760
My people do not want a repeat of the second impact either.

120
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:07,980
You understand that.

121
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:12,000
You mean that everything I've learned about second impact is wrong?

122
00:07:12,360 --> 00:07:12,700
Yes.

123
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:16,340
The history books say that it was a disaster caused by a massive meteorite.

124
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:20,280
But most of the true facts have been concealed through international government cover-ups.

125
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:25,280
Fifteen years ago, in Antarctica, mankind discovered the being known as the first angel.

126
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:29,860
In the middle of the investigation, however, for unknown reasons, the angel exploded.

127
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:32,160
That is the real truth about the second impact.

128
00:07:35,740 --> 00:07:38,320
Then the things we're doing here are...

129
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:41,200
Are to prevent a probable third impact before it happens.

130
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:44,740
That is the sole purpose of Nerve and the Evangelions.

131
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:48,780
By the way, Masato, the event will occur tomorrow as scheduled.

132
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:50,900
I understand.

133
00:07:50,900 --> 00:08:04,860
Good morning.

134
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:07,280
Good morning, Masato.

135
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:09,120
I'm going to old Tokyo on business.

136
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:12,800
I'll probably be getting back late tonight, so have something delivered for dinner.

137
00:08:13,380 --> 00:08:13,660
Bye.

138
00:08:15,320 --> 00:08:15,880
Okay.

139
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:17,280
Um, sure.

140
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:35,580
It's hard to believe that this place used to be the flourishing capital known as Tokyo.

141
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:36,580
We're here.

142
00:08:36,940 --> 00:08:37,080
Hmm?

143
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:40,000
Why are they having this in a place like this?

144
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:41,880
Is the SSDF getting involved?

145
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:43,880
The Strategic Self-Defense Force?

146
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:44,460
No.

147
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:45,720
They're not allowed to interfere.

148
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:46,600
I see.

149
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,340
That's why they can do whatever they like.

150
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:59,460
Thank you.

151
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:00,220
Thank you.

152
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:08,020
I'd like to thank you all for coming to this special demonstration of Japan Heavy Chemical Industrial Cooperative's latest product.

153
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:13,700
In a few minutes, we'll be taking you up to the control room to observe the actual demonstration.

154
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:17,100
But first, we'll be answering some of your questions here.

155
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:17,420
Yes.

156
00:09:17,880 --> 00:09:20,220
Ah, the famous Dr. Ritsuko Akagi.

157
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:22,940
It's our pleasure to have you here for this demonstration.

158
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:23,860
Thank you.

159
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:25,200
May I ask you a question?

160
00:09:25,660 --> 00:09:26,240
Of course.

161
00:09:26,460 --> 00:09:26,840
Certainly.

162
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:30,060
The unit is equipped with an internal nuclear reactor.

163
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:30,900
Is this correct?

164
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:31,440
Correct.

165
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:37,780
This is our product's most distinguished feature, guaranteeing 150 days of continuous operating power.

166
00:09:37,780 --> 00:09:38,900
I see.

167
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:46,260
But from a safety perspective, isn't it rather risky to incorporate a nuclear reactor in a land-based weapon designed for hand-to-hand combat?

168
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:50,420
We think it's more practical than a weapon that won't work for more than five minutes.

169
00:09:50,540 --> 00:09:53,580
But in an emergency, there would be problems with remote control.

170
00:09:53,640 --> 00:09:59,240
But it's more humane than a system that induces tremendous mental stress and causes mental instability in the pilot.

171
00:09:59,480 --> 00:09:59,960
Quiet out.

172
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:01,060
You're acting like children.

173
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:03,260
And there's still the issue of manual control.

174
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:11,080
I would think that it is much safer than an extremely dangerous weapon that's been known to run out of control and go berserk in the middle of a city.

175
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:13,680
A weapon that cannot be controlled is insane.

176
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,260
It's like an hysterical woman.

177
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:17,000
Completely out of control.

178
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:22,180
Our technology will be able to control it.

179
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:26,900
So you're saying that science and human courage will tame the savage Ava beast?

180
00:10:27,020 --> 00:10:28,020
Are you serious?

181
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:29,640
Yes, of course I'm serious.

182
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:37,240
And because it depends on something as fragile as a human heart, NERV has allowed the situation to get completely out of control.

183
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:42,680
The UN has already had to approve an enormous supplement to your existing budget.

184
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:48,200
And as a result, 20,000 people in a dozen countries are starving to death.

185
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:51,580
Of course, the actual cause of all this is still under investigation.

186
00:10:52,060 --> 00:10:54,800
Why don't you at least take responsibility for your handiwork?

187
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:58,140
How fortunate that your organization is above the law.

188
00:10:58,420 --> 00:10:59,680
It doesn't matter what you say.

189
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:03,100
The fact is that NERV has the only weapon capable of defeating the enemy.

190
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:04,880
You mean the AT field.

191
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:07,060
That is simply a matter of time and research.

192
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,740
NERV's day in the sun will not last forever.

193
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:15,900
Damn him!

194
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:19,880
Those jokes are just pissed off about being cut out of their share of the loot!

195
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:24,940
I want to rip off that smug face of his and shove it into this locker!

196
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:28,300
Then I'll kick it and kick it and kick it!

197
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:29,820
Put that out.

198
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:30,740
Behave yourself.

199
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:33,700
He's just a show-off, begging for praise and adulation.

200
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:36,220
He's petty, not worthy of attention.

201
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:39,360
Yeah, but how did that smug SOB know about the AT field?

202
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:41,240
How could something so classified leak out?

203
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,620
Intelligence must be dragging its ass.

204
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:59,140
We are ready to begin the jet alone activation test.

205
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:00,540
Don't worry, folks.

206
00:12:00,740 --> 00:12:02,440
There is no risk at all.

207
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:06,640
Please, make yourselves comfortable and watch through the observation window.

208
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:08,100
We are ready to begin.

209
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:09,780
Let's start the test.

210
00:12:10,260 --> 00:12:11,560
Discharging the power core.

211
00:12:11,620 --> 00:12:12,780
Pressure levels normal.

212
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:15,160
Coolant system circulation normal.

213
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,440
Release the control rods.

214
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:19,100
The reactor has reached nominal power status.

215
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:20,380
Output is normal.

216
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:22,140
Begin walk cycle.

217
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:23,700
Walking forward ahead.

218
00:12:23,940 --> 00:12:24,240
Slow.

219
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:25,540
Forward right leg.

220
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:26,160
Roger.

221
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:26,780
Walk.

222
00:12:27,140 --> 00:12:28,100
Forward ahead slow.

223
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:29,840
Forward right leg.

224
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:34,780
Balance is nominal.

225
00:12:35,020 --> 00:12:36,340
Power core status nominal.

226
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:36,940
Roger.

227
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,200
Now, forward left leg.

228
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:40,180
Keep us steady.

229
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:40,780
Roger.

230
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:41,960
Forward left leg.

231
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,080
Maintaining balance.

232
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:43,740
Oh, boy.

233
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:44,740
It's walking.

234
00:12:45,220 --> 00:12:46,880
That's certainly something to be proud of.

235
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:48,960
Wow.

236
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:50,760
What's wrong?

237
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:51,480
This is odd.

238
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:53,440
The pressure inside the reactor is increasing.

239
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:56,260
The temperature of the primary cooling system is also rising.

240
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:57,600
Valve open.

241
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:59,660
Insert the neutron deceleration fluid.

242
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:00,360
No effect.

243
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:02,360
The pump output isn't increasing.

244
00:13:02,580 --> 00:13:04,000
Initiating valve system check.

245
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:06,260
All right.

246
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:07,280
Emergency stop.

247
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:08,100
Cut off the power.

248
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:09,860
Abort signal transmission confirmed.

249
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:11,780
It's not accepting it.

250
00:13:11,980 --> 00:13:13,440
The radio circuit is being blocked.

251
00:13:13,620 --> 00:13:14,620
It's out of control.

252
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:15,940
This can't be happening.

253
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:17,440
It's coming right at us.

254
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:18,300
Oh, my God.

255
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:22,280
Oh, my God.

256
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:22,820
Oh, my God.

257
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:33,460
This robot's as badly behaved as the idiot who built it.

258
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:40,200
The compression valve is operating irregularly.

259
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:41,620
The control rods aren't working.

260
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:43,660
Possibility of meltdown imminent.

261
00:13:44,540 --> 00:13:45,140
Impossible.

262
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:50,880
The jet alone's onboard computer system has been programmed to handle all possible contingencies

263
00:13:50,880 --> 00:13:51,600
and scenarios.

264
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:54,780
This kind of thing simply cannot happen.

265
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:58,160
Well, then, you're about to have an impossible nuclear meltdown out there.

266
00:13:58,620 --> 00:14:02,860
Under the present circumstances, our only viable option is to wait for it to stop itself.

267
00:14:03,060 --> 00:14:04,520
And how likely is that?

268
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:07,080
0.0002%.

269
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,340
It would be an act of God.

270
00:14:08,420 --> 00:14:10,440
Acts of men are better than acts of God.

271
00:14:10,580 --> 00:14:11,980
Tell me how to stop that thing.

272
00:14:12,140 --> 00:14:14,820
We've already tried every possible option.

273
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:15,400
Not yet.

274
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:16,760
There's got to be a last resort.

275
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:17,960
A way to wipe out everything.

276
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:19,000
Tell me the password.

277
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,840
The password to delete all programming is top secret.

278
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:23,820
I don't have the authority to release it.

279
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:26,480
I'm sorry, but I'm not allowed to tell you.

280
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:28,260
Then you better get the clearance, Vato.

281
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:29,360
Do it!

282
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:31,460
Tukita here.

283
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:33,520
Let me speak to Mr. Manda in Tokyo, too.

284
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:34,400
That's right.

285
00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:36,120
The Director of Internal Affairs.

286
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:38,800
Well, I'll have to delegate that to Mr. Yasugi.

287
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:39,640
Ask him.

288
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:44,740
Well, I can't give you authorization for such an important matter verbally.

289
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,520
Could you submit a written request?

290
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:49,480
So now I need to get Mr. Yoshizawa's permission?

291
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:50,600
What?

292
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:53,300
Yes, I've already gotten approval from Mr. Witts.

293
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:53,960
Yes.

294
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:54,520
Yes.

295
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:55,140
Okay.

296
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:56,320
Bureaucracies.

297
00:14:56,860 --> 00:14:58,660
A written order of clearance will be sent.

298
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:00,240
I'll give you the password then.

299
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:01,820
We can't wait that long!

300
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:03,900
Watch Jettelone's reactor red lines.

301
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:04,660
It'll be too late.

302
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:10,820
Jettelone is heading for Atsugi City.

303
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:12,880
Time's running out.

304
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:15,820
I'm taking the responsibility for this operation myself.

305
00:15:16,140 --> 00:15:17,300
You can wait here.

306
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:22,420
Yuga, I want you to roll out the transport and bring Shinji and Unit 1 with the F equipment

307
00:15:22,420 --> 00:15:23,420
up here right now.

308
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:24,640
Yes, this is an emergency.

309
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:25,840
This is pointless.

310
00:15:26,220 --> 00:15:27,580
Call this off, Captain Katsuragi.

311
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:29,920
Do you have any idea as to how to stop it?

312
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:32,120
I'll override the computer manually.

313
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:36,560
Are you serious?

314
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:37,320
Yes.

315
00:15:37,780 --> 00:15:41,000
But Jettelone's interior must be flooded with radiation.

316
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:42,160
You're insane.

317
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:44,660
But if I succeed, Atsugi will be saved.

318
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:50,400
The access hatch can be opened manually as soon as our command signal is cut off.

319
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:53,120
You should be able to enter the hatch through the backpack unit.

320
00:15:53,140 --> 00:15:53,520
Mm-hmm.

321
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:55,640
Hope.

322
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:59,200
That's the password to delete the programming.

323
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:01,120
Thank you, sir.

324
00:16:07,020 --> 00:16:08,700
Our target is Jettelone.

325
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:11,540
There's a danger that it may begin to melt down in five minutes.

326
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:14,800
Therefore, we cannot allow it to get any closer to a populated area.

327
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:15,540
Yuga.

328
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:16,340
Yes, ma'am.

329
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:20,440
As soon as you drop Unit 1, take the transport up to a safe altitude and stand by.

330
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:20,880
Roger.

331
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,120
And Shinji.

332
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:22,420
Yes.

333
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:25,140
Run alongside the target and place me onto its back.

334
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:28,980
Once I've gotten on, I want you to try to hold Jettelone back as much as you can.

335
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,480
You're climbing on that thing?

336
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:31,560
To break into it?

337
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:32,480
That's right.

338
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:33,880
But that's just crazy.

339
00:16:34,140 --> 00:16:34,640
I know.

340
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:37,300
But I'm afraid there just isn't any better way to stop it.

341
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:38,480
But it's too dangerous.

342
00:16:38,900 --> 00:16:39,700
Don't worry.

343
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:43,060
Unit 1's armor can handle both the explosion and the radiation.

344
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:43,840
Not for Ava.

345
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:45,240
I meant for you.

346
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:48,020
Well, I've got to give it my best shot, you know.

347
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:50,100
My conscience won't let me do otherwise.

348
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:54,840
Ma'am, I've sighted the target.

349
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:59,720
Right.

350
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:00,600
Here we go.

351
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:06,420
Ava approaching drop position.

352
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:08,060
Docking release.

353
00:17:08,320 --> 00:17:08,620
Roger.

354
00:17:24,840 --> 00:17:28,740
We caught up with it.

355
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:30,200
We've got less than four minutes.

356
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:31,220
Put me on now.

357
00:17:41,780 --> 00:17:42,920
Don't think about it.

358
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:43,480
Do it.

359
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:51,320
Misano.

360
00:17:54,840 --> 00:18:17,520
I found it.

361
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:17,580
I found it.

362
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:33,520
Error?

363
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:34,560
What the hell?

364
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:42,320
The program must have been altered.

365
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:43,460
It must have.

366
00:18:49,460 --> 00:18:52,640
The power reactor is just 0.2 point short of critical.

367
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:55,160
The control rod still won't function.

368
00:18:55,540 --> 00:18:57,060
I guess I'll try the long shot.

369
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:16,000
Misano!

370
00:19:16,380 --> 00:19:17,220
Get out of there!

371
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:18,420
I'm so scared.

372
00:19:18,820 --> 00:19:19,660
Dammit!

373
00:19:19,820 --> 00:19:20,440
Die!

374
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:20,900
I'm so scared.

375
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:25,620
Misano!

376
00:19:30,620 --> 00:19:32,160
0.1 to critical.

377
00:19:32,460 --> 00:19:33,880
My God, it's going to go.

378
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:34,960
Meltdown imminent.

379
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:35,940
All safety's failing.

380
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:36,300
Dear God.

381
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:37,100
Misano!

382
00:19:37,100 --> 00:19:37,340
Misano!

383
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:37,720
Misano!

384
00:19:37,720 --> 00:20:01,720
She did it!

385
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:02,720
Internal pressure lowering.

386
00:20:02,720 --> 00:20:04,720
All readings are nominal.

387
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:05,720
Yes!

388
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:09,720
Yes, she did it!

389
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:11,720
Crazy fool.

390
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,720
Misato, are you all right?

391
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:14,720
Misato!

392
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:16,720
Yeah, I'm okay.

393
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:18,720
Not in the greatest of shape, however.

394
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:19,720
You're alive!

395
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:20,720
Oh, God!

396
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:22,720
Are you all right?

397
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:23,720
Oh, thank God!

398
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:24,720
I can't believe you did it!

399
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:26,720
It's a miracle!

400
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:32,720
Yeah, but the miracle was set up by someone.

401
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:36,720
Recovery of Unit 1 is completed.

402
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:38,720
No danger of radioactive contamination.

403
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:40,720
Except for Captain Katsuragi's operation.

404
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:42,720
Everything went according to the plan.

405
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:44,720
Good work.

406
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:54,720
Good morning, Shinji.

407
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:56,720
That's the way to start your morning.

408
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:57,720
Now, let me out that shower.

409
00:20:57,720 --> 00:21:11,720
Hey, Shinji, have you seen any clean bras or panties lying around?

410
00:21:11,720 --> 00:21:13,720
Good morning, Ikari!

411
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:14,720
Good morning, Ikari!

412
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:15,720
Hmm?

413
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:16,720
Morning.

414
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:18,720
I'm taking off!

415
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:19,720
Have a nice day!

416
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:24,720
Misato is just so cool.

417
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:26,720
Yeah, I used to think so, too.

418
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:28,720
But she's such a slob.

419
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:29,720
She's always embarrassing me.

420
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:32,720
She never does anything but lie around the house.

421
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:35,720
She's not embarrassed about it, but I am.

422
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:38,720
You're a lucky guy.

423
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:41,720
What do you mean?

424
00:21:41,720 --> 00:21:44,720
Ikari really is just a kid, isn't he?

425
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:45,720
He sure is.

426
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:46,720
Meaning what?

427
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:50,720
She let you see a side of her that she wouldn't show to anyone else, right?

428
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:52,720
That means she's your family.

429
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:53,720
Yeah.

430
00:21:53,720 --> 00:22:09,720
Fly me to the moon and let me play among the stars.

431
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:17,720
Let me see what's bling is like on Jupiter and Mars.

432
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:25,720
In other words, hold my hand.

433
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:33,720
In other words, darling, kiss me.

434
00:22:33,720 --> 00:22:42,720
Be my heartless song and let me sing forever more.

435
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:49,720
You are all I long for, all I worship and adore.

436
00:22:49,720 --> 00:22:57,720
In other words, please be true.

437
00:22:57,720 --> 00:23:05,720
In other words, I love you.

438
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:09,720
Get ready to meet Eva Unit 2 and its pilot as they head towards Japan.

439
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:12,720
Will Shinji be able to handle this loud and pushy redhead?

440
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:13,720
Or is his ship already sunk?

441
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:18,720
Things get worse when a new angel surprise attack forces them to activate Unit 2 in the Eva's first undersea battle.

442
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:20,720
Don't miss, Asuka strikes!

